With all this talk of Minesweeper levels, Pacman levels, Pong
levels... I thought I'd bring up my favorite other-game level idea:
Robots levels.

I mean the old terminal game "robots" often distributed with BSD and
Linux (also known as "daleks" [1]).

The idea is basically that you're in a big open room. There are a
bunch of robots around. On each turn, the robots move one step towards
you. If one of them hits you, it will kill you. They are pretty much
indestructible, except if two of them run into each other, in which
case they are both destroyed a leave a trash pile which will destroy
any further robots that run into it. The objective is to move around
in such a way that the robots all bump into one another and destroy
each other. (In some versions you have a one-shot 'sonic-screwdriver'
which will kill all robots in the 8 neighbouring squares).

Anyhow, I thought this wouldn't be too hard to make into a nethack
level. Perhaps you could make the outcomes less severe - not
instadeath, but significant amounts of damage. And maybe they aren't
completely impervious to damage either. And of course, this being
nethack, there are lots of other ways to avoid the robots, or trap
them, or confuse them, or ...

One of these days I'll a have a go at coding this.

